tellate cells. They differentiate into fibrogenic myofibroblasts during chronic injury states producing high levels of collagen.\")\n\n  Line 24178: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0009100 \"portal fibroblast\")\n\n  Line 24179: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009100 \"hepatic portal fibroblast\")\n\n  Line 24182: # Class: obo:CL_0009101 (fibroblastic reticular cell)\n\n  Line 24188: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009101 \"fibroblastic reticular cell\")\n\n  Line 24193: # Class: obo:CL_0009102 (lymph node fibroblastic reticular cell)\n\n  Line 24195: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21435450\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22566825\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25998961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28262465\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29752062\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34256989\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009102 \"A specialized, fibroblastic reticular cell of mesenchymal origin found in lymph nodes. In human, it expresses several markers common to myofibroblasts (desmin, vimentin, CD73, CD90, α-smooth muscle actin (αSMA)), and can be differentiated from endothelial cells by its lack of CD31 expression. These cells are critical for the overall organization and function of the lymph node. Lymph node fibroblastic reticular cells (FRCs) can be further classified based on their location, function, and unique marker expression.\")\n\n  Line 24199: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0009102 \"fibroblastic reticular cell\")\n\n  Line 24200: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009102 \"lymph node fibroblastic reticular cell\")\n\n  Line 24206: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21435450\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22566825\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25998961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28262465\") Annotation(oboInO